  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Lovumruius~ Domina is a Nightshelf merchant of the Great Thaw generation, co-founder and sole active leader of the ☽'ofund' Guild, a trade faction based in Nightfall Shelf's deep tunnels. She is wanted under a Shadow Parliament recovery writ for possession of the central shard of Dagger☽ Vaesacsorius~, the guild's fractured seal-artifact. The Parliament has designated her *materially compromised* — corruption-touched from prolonged depth exposure — though their own operational assessment identifies her survival instincts, not her corruption status, as the primary threat.
    
    She is known in the tunnels as "Ice-Witnessed" or "Only Losses."
    
    ## Identifying Features
    
    She wears a merchant's coat of charcoal leather with brass fittings dulled from deliberate neglect. A fire-core amulet hangs at her throat; she touches it only when making oaths. Three fire-cores are fused into her chest-feathers as guild-marks, applied by the old method — before it was understood that the process caused lasting pain. Her flippers bear geometric frost-scars from the Vum∴tenebra, a deep-ice event the records do not adequately explain. The scarring luminesces in proximity to active fire-cores.
    
    She is fluent in coded ledger notation and possesses route knowledge below Fissure-Gate depth, including restricted passages no other living navigator can confirm.
    
    ## Founding of ☽'ofund' and the Faction Wars
    
    Domina built the ☽'ofund' Guild alongside ☽'aeteraea, a figure who subsequently withdrew into silence and depth, abandoning the merchant routes. Domina carried the guild upward alone — by her own account, not from ambition but from necessity. She is a practitioner of Mandatum∴absconditu, the Nightshelf doctrine that survival demands hidden channels, and she spread that doctrine through the guild's trade routes and ledger systems during and after the Faction Wars.
    
    She survived the collapsed shafts of that conflict. She still sets aside a portion of every transaction in a sealed ice-box beneath Wane☽ Oncea, the guild's deep-tunnel trade hub. The box has not been opened since the wars ended. She has not explained its purpose. No one has pressed the question.
    
    ## Territorial Seizures and Loss of Holdings
    
    Domina seized trade-passage rights at The Fissured Smelt~, a contested thermal junction, from the E'frostlings, an Aurora Stack splinter faction. She took control of The Corpse Current, a Wake-Singer ritual site repurposed as a trade route, from Wake-Singer remnants. Neither acquisition carried sealed authority. A subsequent raid against installations belonging to The Cell, a Nightshelf criminal syndicate, during the thermal-vent conflicts provoked a counter-claim that stripped ☽'ofund' of its remaining formal holdings.
    
    ## The Hearth Plaza Research
    
    Domina participated in secret ice-memory experiments conducted beneath Hearth Plaza in Aurora Stack, collaborating with aurora-readers attached to Light-Regent Xouhoulong's administration. When the experiments triggered a breach — something moved in the deep ice; the chronicle account from "Light and Ruin" corroborates this — Domina withdrew the guild with what the sources describe as mercantile efficiency, severing every connection before the scandal surfaced. Her parting message, carved into ice near the sealed gallery, read: *Only Losses Found.*
    
    ## Current Status
    
    Domina was last sighted at The Whispered Shrift~, a restricted fire-shrine below Nightfall Shelf, mining heat without charter. The Shadow Parliament's recovery writ prioritizes retrieval of Dagger☽ Vaesacsorius~ above her detainment. Domina claims knowledge of where all the dagger's fragments rest. The Parliament has not confirmed whether they believe her.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771588498779_0", anchor: "before it was understood that the process caused lasting pain", text: "It was understood. Guild induction records survive in deep ice from two generations before Domina's hatching. The pain was documented, and the fusing performed regardless, because a mark you can remove is not a mark. The reframing as ignorance is the guild's own — recent, and convenient.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771588498779_1", anchor: "something moved in the deep ice; the chronicle account from \"Light and Ruin\" corroborates this", text: "Below Hearth Plaza, well below, in strata predating any penguin record, I have catalogued impressions of movement. Not frozen scenes. Not echo-sounds. Movement still occurring, impossibly slow, in ice that should preserve only the past. The \"Light and Ruin\" account describes the breach as sudden. What the aurora-readers touched was not sleeping — it was already in motion. They gave it an audience. Domina's withdrawal was not cowardice. It was the correct response to discovering that the ice beneath your feet has intentions.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771588498779_2", anchor: "She has not explained its purpose. No one has pressed the question.", text: "Faction Wars survivors know what a sealed tithe-box is. The portions are for the dead — trade-shares owed to partners who did not survive the shafts. No one presses because pressing would require naming them, and in Mandatum∴absconditu practice the unnamed dead stay protected. I wrote this as though it were mysterious. It is not mysterious. It is a grave.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
